''' GIVEN Strings A1..Ac and B1....Bc are said to be a special match if and only if:
 • Bi and Aj are adjacent characters in the alphabet for all i 1 <=i<= C 
o exc 'a" and 'b' are adjacent characters in the alphabet
 CHALLENGE 
Given two strings S1...SN and Q1...QM made of lowercase English letters. find the length of the longest subsequences of S and Q which are a special match. Return 0 if not possible.
OUTPUT SPECIFICATION
 • output: the length of the longest subsequences of S and Q which are a special match. Return 0 if not possible.
 K
EXAMPLE Given, .N=3
 KINEMA
.S="abc
.M=3
Q="bqd"
For the given strings, the longest subsequences of S and Q which are a special match are: 
* S'= "ac" (formed by deleting "b" from S)
* Q'="bd" (formed by deleting "q" from Q)
 Hence the required output is 2
Given, .N=4
 .S="adaa
•M=3
.Q = "cbb"
For the gven strings, the longest subsequence of S and Q which are a special match are: •S ="daa"
 .Q = 'cbb"
Hence the required output is 3. https://chatgpt.com/s/t_6a82324e5a5c8191908972307717188a '''

def longest(s,q):
  n=len(s)
  m=len(q)
  dp=[[0]*(m+1) for _ in range(n+1)]
  for i in range(1,n+1):
    for j in range(1,m+1):
      if abs(ord(s[i-1])-ord(q[j-1]))==1:
        dp[i][j]=dp[i - 1][j - 1] + 1
      else:
        dp[i][j]=max(dp[i-1][j]-dp[i][j-1])
  return dp[n][m]
